=== layout: two-panels

# X-0 system

@left

- In grasshoppers, cockroaches, and some other insects, X is the only type of sex chromosome.
- Females are XX; males have one X (X0).
- The sperm contributes an X chromosome or no sex chromosome.

@right

![X-0 system](assets/lect06d-x_linked_genes_1/xo_system.svg)

@notes

Source: lect06d-x_linked_genes_1.odp, slide 21. Replacement reason: normalized distributed pictorial annotations into native source-order content; normalized overlapping legacy components into one native source-order panel | Imported content for reconstruction: | Original layout: one-panel | # X-O System | Original slot: body | ![Slide image 13](assets/lect06d-x_linked_genes_1/image_013.png) | - (b) The X-0 system | - 22 + X | - 22 + XX | - In grasshoppers, cockroaches, and some other insects, there is only one type of sex chromosome, the X. | - Females are XX; | - males have only one sex chromosome (X0). | - Sex of the offspring is [determined by the sperm cell]{color=red} and whether it contains an X chromosome or no sex chromosome.

