@question

In birds, sex is determined by a ZW chromosome scheme.
Males are ZZ and females are ZW.
A recessive lethal allele that causes death of the embryo is sometimes present on the Z chromosome in pigeons.
What would be the sex ratio in the offspring of a cross between a male that is heterozygous for the lethal allele and a wild type female?

- A) 2\:1 male to female
- B) 1\:2 male to female
- C) 1\:1 male to female
- D) 3\:1 male to female

@answer

